meta {
  name: Create Order
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/order
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "items": [
      {
        "productId": "{{productId}}",
        "quantity": 2
      }
    ]
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body.id) {
    bru.setVar("orderId", res.body.id);
  }
}

docs {
  Full chain required, in order: auth-service/Register.bru + Login.bru (needs
  {{accessToken}}), auth-service/Login Admin.bru (needs {{adminAccessToken}}),
  product-service/Create Product.bru (needs {{productId}}), and
  inventory-service/Insert Inventory Item.bru with skuCode = {{productId}} (needs at
  least 2 units in stock).

  eureka-server, product-service, inventory-service and order-service must ALL be
  running and registered — OrderService.createOrder() calls product-service via
  OpenFeign (ProductClient, lb://product-service) to price each item, then calls
  inventory-service via OpenFeign (InventoryClient.reserve, lb://inventory-service) to
  atomically decrement stock, BEFORE saving the order. If either call fails, the order
  is never persisted. RabbitMQ should also be running (order-service publishes
  OrderEventDTO to order.exchange/order.created after saving) but a broker outage
  doesn't block the HTTP response itself — this API has no outbox/retry, see CLAUDE.md.

  userId is NOT taken from the request body — it's derived from the JWT subject
  (authentication.getName(), i.e. the logged-in user's email), unlike account-service's
  legacy behavior in the FraudShield sibling project. Run against "Gateway" (any
  authenticated user) or "OrderDirect" — unlike product/inventory-service,
  order-service DOES validate the JWT itself even when hit directly (OrderSecurityFilter
  + SecurityConfig.anyRequest().authenticated()), so OrderDirect without a token also
  401s. See order-service-errors/Create Order No Token.bru.

  Saves {{orderId}}. Order is born with status CONFIRMED immediately (no
  payment-service in this project — see CLAUDE.md).

  Expected: 201 CREATED with the order (status CONFIRMED, totalValue = price × qty
  summed across items, items[] with productName/price snapshotted at order time).
}
